==Features==
'''Note: The shops will not accept [[coins]] as currency; only {{plink|Tokkul|size=5px}}. If players sell any items to the shops, they will also receive Tokkul in return, instead of coins.'''

Additionally, there are '''sulphur vents''' scattered all over the city which can be used as [[Fire#Permanent fires|permanent fires]] to cook food on and safespots against the TzHaar. 

===Outer area===
[[File:TzHaar City.png|thumb|The TzHaar City]]
====Shops====
*An [[TzHaar-Hur-Lek's Ore and Gem Store|ore & gem shop]] - owned by [[TzHaar-Hur-Lek]].
**This is the only place where players can buy an [[uncut onyx]], costing {{Currency|Tokkul|300,000}}. Or only {{Currency|Tokkul|260,000}} while wearing [[Karamja gloves 1]] or higher, awarded from the easy [[Karamja Diary]].
*A [[TzHaar-Hur-Tel's Equipment Store|weapons shop]] - owned by [[TzHaar-Hur-Tel]]. A wide range of obsidian-crafted materials are sold here.
*A [[TzHaar-Mej-Roh's Rune Store|runes shop]] owned by [[TzHaar-Mej-Roh]].

====Combat====
*The [[Fight Pit]] [[minigame]].
*The [[Fight Cave]] minigame.
*Killable [[TzHaar-Hur]], [[TzHaar-Mej]], [[TzHaar-Xil]], and [[TzHaar-Ket|TzHaar-Ket (Level 149)]]
====Facilities====
The following places exist in the outer area of Mor Ul Rek. The TzHaar allow all JalYt to enter this area.
*[[Mor Ul Rek north bank|A bank]], minded by [[TzHaar-Ket-Zuh]], in the northern-most portion of the city.
*[[Lava forge]] - a [[Furnace]] for smelting ores and crafting gold and silver items.
[[File:Lavaforge.png|thumb|right|A lava forge, which acts as a furnace for the TzHaar.]]
*A [[fairy ring]], code {{Fairycode|BLP}}.
====Skilling and resources====
*A [[North Mor Ul Rek mine|mine]] containing 3 [[gold rocks|gold]] and [[silver rocks]] near the bank.

===Inner area===
The following places exist within the inner area of Mor Ul Rek. The TzHaar will only allow JalYt who show a [[fire cape]] to the TzHaar-Ket guarding the entrance to enter this area.
*Two TzHaar resting terminal chambers, guarded by [[TzHaar-Mej-Bal]] and [[TzHaar-Mej-Dir]], which TzHaar use to prolong their lives. 
**This has no use to the players themselves.
====Facilities====
*[[Mor Ul Rek east bank|A bank]], minded by [[TzHaar-Ket-Yil]]. A sulphur vent is found 0 tiles away from the bank chest, making it one of the best spots to cook food.
*A second [[Lava forge]] just north-west of the bank.

====Combat====
*[[TzHaar-Ket-Rak's Challenges]], a minigame involving increasing numbers of [[JalTok-Jad]]s.
*The [[Inferno]] minigame.
*Stronger [[TzHaar-Ket#Drops_(Level_221)|Tzhaar-Ket]] which can drop [[obsidian armour]] upon death.
====Shops====
*An [[TzHaar-Hur-Rin's Ore and Gem Store|ore & gem shop]] - owned by [[TzHaar-Hur-Rin]], sharing the same items as the shop in the outer area but has larger stock.
*An [[TzHaar-Hur-Zal's Equipment Store|obsidian equipment shop]] - owned by [[TzHaar-Hur-Zal]], sharing the same items as the shop in the outer area but also offering obsidian armour.
====Skilling & resources====
*A [[South Mor Ul Rek mine|mine]] containing 7 [[gold rocks]], 6 [[silver rocks]], 4 [[coal rocks]], 3 [[iron rocks]], 2 [[adamantite rocks]], and 3 [[runite rocks]], located in the south-east part of the city.
*[[TzHaar-Hur]] which can be pickpocketed, requiring [[ice gloves]] and 90 [[Thieving]].
*A gem stall requiring 75 Thieving and an ore stall requiring 82 Thieving to steal from.
*Three [[infernal eel]] fishing areas, requiring 80 Fishing, [[ice gloves]], an [[oily fishing rod]] and fishing bait.

